**Languages.** Write {% if review %}the issue draft and the ADR (an intent file){% else %}the intent file and the GitHub issue draft{% endif %} in English: they are the shared
record and GitHub's. After every write to an intent file ({% if review %}step 6{% else %}steps 4 and 6{% endif %}), also write its
**reading copy**: `.claude/intent/view/<the intent file's name, lowercased>`, the whole file
translated into {{ copies[0].language }}{% for c in copies[1:] %}, and `.claude/intent/view/<that name without .md>.{{ c.suffix }}.md`, translated into {{ c.language }}{% endfor %}, with the same structure — code, paths, identifiers, `file:line` and @mentions left
as they are. Write it with the Write or Edit tool (a Bash write doesn't trigger the page): ocgen
renders it as a page beside the intent file's, with a switch between the languages, and opens it —
never write the `.html` yourself. ocgen reminds you when a copy falls behind its intent file. The
copy is git-ignored; the English intent file is the record.